 Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q38SD2","text":"Serine/threonine-protein kinase which phosphorylates RAB proteins involved in intracellular trafficking (PubMed:36040231). Phosphorylates RAB7A; this activity is dependent on protein kinase C (PKC) activation (PubMed:36040231, PubMed:37558661, PubMed:37857821). Plays a role in the negative regulation of bone mass, acting through the maturation of osteoclasts (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}